<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:22:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Real questions to be asked' after deadly train collision in Spain, journalist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b79bf0d1907a6d3fe2ebfe3592d98ff1efd822f69c80360afbb7c0532d2e336f</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:44:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says--1490159b0812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we focus on the tragic train collision that killed at least 68 people in Spain on Wednesday. We're joined by Nicholas Kingsley, executive editor of Railway Gazette International.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>France: Trappes racist shooting suspect transferred to French court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e99f03792c2623568fc6020cd37aba129cd139affb7aaf6bd0b253bc41c2a28a</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court--154349787262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court" /><summary type="html">French anti-terrorism prosecutor Olivier Christen said the suspect in the Trappes racist attack, which killed one person and injured five others, had been brought before a French court. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Very disturbing details': Trappes shooting suspect admits targeting victims by race, religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bca60c14ae0f30f28f8185464f7308881aa967e6eb4c49210e5e0869c914d66f</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:10:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion--8ff667bcd1eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion" /><summary type="html">A man suspected of a gun attack in the Paris suburbs last week that killed one person and wounded five including a child has admitted to "targeting individuals who appeared to be Muslim, African, or North African," prosecutors said on Thursday. FRANCE 24's Charli James reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain begins three days of mourning after train crash kills 69</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fc22abc1a4688fd164e36a44d4a97feef381e19fe8ced5517e5b4aa58d6a867</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:01:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69--a6afb8b3d275.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69" /><summary type="html">Spain's second high-speed rail disaster this year, in which one train struck another from behind, killing 69 people, has raised fresh concerns about the safety of the country's rail network ahead of a national election. Three days of mourning have begun in the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's train crash kills 69 people: What exactly happened?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efdb54344629cc435de45d9fa6a925f74514b9e037c6943503de0a02293969ae</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:53:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened--724a6701ea5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened" /><summary type="html">In Spain, the deadly train accident that killed 69 people and injured scores has once again brought national railway safety under the spotlight. Spain’s transport minister reported an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to one of Europe's deadliest train disasters this century.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 13 killed in 'horrific' Russian drone strike at Ukraine train station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c3de7cdc326bf4f8d9e92a01bf67529e89d161b25888dd716c727f30ac4ca0e</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T11:36:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station--6f3d27577414.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station" /><summary type="html">At least 13 people were killed when a Russian drone struck a busy railway station in Ukraine's Dnipro on Thursday, President Volodymyr Zelensky said, describing the attack as "horrific" and urging Kyiv's allies not to ease sanctions on Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French anti-terrorism prosecutor gives press conference on racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b420b906e2728165415b38a2634eacd7f2ab0fc5166a9f4eb2e74b542e8cad52</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:56:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack--d3a956ca5cd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor, Olivier Christen, gave a press conference on Thursday about the recent racist terrorist attack that killed one man and wounded five others, including a 12-year-old girl, in Trappes. Watch our replay.</summary></entry><entry><title>ECB President Christine Lagarde to step down in February 2027, nine months before term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f885a16a87b968b53e44edd3d1518471428257985bdfc25a5ec702952126a4c3</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:22:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:21:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-ecb-president-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-2027-nine-months-before-term-ends--9e616059c691.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-ecb-president-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-2027-nine-months-before-term-ends" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde will step down on February 7, 2027, nearly nine months before her term expires, the ECB said Thursday. Her successor will be appointed by the European Council under EU treaty rules.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Desolation, despair': Spain begins three days of mourning after deadly train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b4c763a7d2ace5acec20117dfb73343050bc4b1418bf3cc159099028113caf6</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:22:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T06:25:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-desolation-despair-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-deadly-train-crash--584ebc479bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-desolation-despair-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-deadly-train-crash" /><summary type="html">Spain entered three days of mourning on Thursday after a high-speed train collision killed 69 people and injured scores. The incident has prompted fresh questions about rail safety and management.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU drop associate membership plan in bid to deepen ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8306a4cfffd5c6d6ee4ce8222012efc72a38e44be6afbc41dc508c752833267b</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T00:56:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-canada-and-eu-drop-associate-membership-plan-in-bid-to-deepen-ties--888df042e229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-canada-and-eu-drop-associate-membership-plan-in-bid-to-deepen-ties" /><summary type="html">Canada and the European Union will pursue closer ties but have dropped a proposal for associate EU membership, according to a joint declaration ahead of Thursday’s summit in Montreal. Prime Minister Mark Carney is seeking to reduce Canada’s reliance on the US, despite warnings from Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain rail crash came after train ordered to go in error: minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:622e4d0a005e799b7485a1588f96d7e43115b4c33292784c6b07b988a60696b5</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:30:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-rail-crash-came-after-train-ordered-to-go-in-error-minister--7fd7d68c2adb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-rail-crash-came-after-train-ordered-to-go-in-error-minister" /><summary type="html">A rail collision in Spain that claimed at least 68 lives on Wednesday came after a train was ordered to go in "error" despite a technical failure that halted all services, the transport minister said. The first findings about the accident in the central region of Castilla-La Mancha are likely to revive questions about rail safety in Spain after another high-speed collision in January killed 46 people. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rail safety questioned after Spain suffers second fatal high-speed train crash in a year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31eb041809f1199a8cc501fb14d796fa4f75b739d8b7255471b6cdde92fd9029</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:11:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-rail-safety-questioned-after-spain-suffers-second-fatal-high-speed-train-crash-in-a-year--9c4ef79853c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-rail-safety-questioned-after-spain-suffers-second-fatal-high-speed-train-crash-in-a-year" /><summary type="html">Questions are being raised about Spain's rail safety as authorities launch an official investigation into the cause of Wednesday's high-speed train collision, which killed at least 68 people and wounded around 100 more, in the country's second fatal rail crash this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b4c2c4c5daf961d704b4dafb67b71a9893110702b4e75d45c84019a054aca7f</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:57:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-mot--388c86d76aac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans' Affairs of Ukraine. "If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland," says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9db80278cfc9fc7c81b0fd7e730d47a5628df98d3f019059525c29677ca798e0</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:54:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland--f23de8cc008b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans' Affairs of Ukraine. "If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland," says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain high-speed train crash kills 68, injures over 100</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e36a5a03bf0672f44900aafa035e23eaf0cc8db19adc66c7d387f8920c38f45c</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:32:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100--9e328dc364f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 68 people and injured scores more on Wednesday, with the toll likely to rise, authorities said, in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. The second such accident to strike Spain this year will raise fresh questions about the country's rail safety, with the transport minister speaking of an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to the collision. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Urda, south of Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Racist attack in Trappes deeply scars local community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28b1130ddf841ee4e7d872afa21f00ba0bba97742ec2c548d94c125a7eda3307</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:53:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community--369e58b75191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community" /><summary type="html">It has been five days since a gunman opened fire in the Paris suburb of Trappes in a racist attack that left one person dead and five others injured. Over the weekend, hundreds of people marched through the town to pay tribute to the 26-year-old victim, Bossio Wangi, and show solidarity with his family. The attack has left a deep mark on the local community, and mediators have been mobilised to provide support. Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 64 dead in Spain’s high-speed train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5c808caccf180d9f8eaa3a16e2898db3c9229a78aa6b9be7710590c123b0ffe</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-at-least-64-dead-in-spain-s-high-speed-train-crash--c2c0a9282759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-at-least-64-dead-in-spain-s-high-speed-train-crash" /><summary type="html">At least 64 people died when two Spanish ​high-speed trains collided on Wednesday, with rescue workers scouring the wreckage for more bodies after Spain's second deadly rail accident this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Spanish Transport Minister gives press conference on train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2f36c131fe2f943c0cea9e652ef0de6bb4171679c5bcb1e296683150e78d479</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:43:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-replay-spanish-transport-minister-gives-press-conference-on-train-crash--2513ae4b186c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-replay-spanish-transport-minister-gives-press-conference-on-train-crash" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 64 people and injured scores more on Wednesday (October 28), with the toll likely to rise, authorities said in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente gave some details in a press conference.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: Dozens killed after one high-speed train slams into another</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53045b8c213e2ff2b90d38121f9b38e07cc53d56b6de21714833656b65f2b965</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-dozens-killed-after-one-high-speed-train-slams-into-another--dd4e2815667c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-dozens-killed-after-one-high-speed-train-slams-into-another" /><summary type="html">Spain suffered its second deadly high-speed train accident this year when one train on Wednesday, October 28, slammed into another that had stopped on the tracks, with the impact shredding cars and killing at least 64 people. The accident comes with memories still fresh of another crash between high-speed trains in southern Spain in January. France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris gives us the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: At least 64 dead in high-speed train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4fe2c5a60ea60f38ca7b8dc50de42e9e345c417fb55b7398d53fab3dafde4c3</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:33:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-64-dead-in-high-speed-train-crash--8f3b32d96110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-64-dead-in-high-speed-train-crash" /><summary type="html">In Spain, a high-speed train slammed into the rear of another train that had stopped, derailing two cars and killing at least 64 people on Wednesday, October 28. The central government’s office for Castilla La Mancha confirmed the death toll had risen. It is the second major train accident in Spain this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Melania Trump-brokered local ceasefire holds for second day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bac78b89f22e0d4481266b670cd03c610244680810f989384cd36d8e88f3dee3</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:42:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-melania-trump-brokered-local-ceasefire-holds-for-second-day--3a486bd361a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-melania-trump-brokered-local-ceasefire-holds-for-second-day" /><summary type="html">There ​have been ​no breaches of the US-brokered local ceasefire ​around ‌the ⁠Russian-occupied town of Oleshky ‌in southern Ukraine during its first 30 hours, ​Ukraine's human rights ‌ombudsman Dmytro Lubinets said on ‌Wednesday. A ceasefire has ​been agreed until November 1 to ​allow residents of ​the frontline ​town – who had ​been unable to leave amid near-uninhabitable conditions – to evacuate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Ceasefire holds for its first 30 hours in occupied Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c93415711300fef8e075b2b44439e415b28567cfff88bccf46bfcdfc3c818a4</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-ceasefire-holds-for-its-first-30-hours-in-occupied-oleshky--e81d58d29088.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-ceasefire-holds-for-its-first-30-hours-in-occupied-oleshky" /><summary type="html">A local ceasefire in the Russian-occupied southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky held through its first day and night, despite continued fighting between Moscow and Kyiv elsewhere. The truce, which began on Tuesday in the devastated city, is expected to remain in place until Sunday. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: At least 10 dead in crash between 2 high-speed trains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c96ce4c015df413178507cf7ce72423be9bd91298801134d97ffab48e769232</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-10-dead-in-crash-between-2-high-speed-trains--af73883b4eb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-10-dead-in-crash-between-2-high-speed-trains" /><summary type="html">At least ten people have died in a crash between two trains in central Spain. The crash occurred Wednesday morning  in the province of Toledo. Rail service is suspended between Madrid, Ciudad Real and Andalusia.
 
France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain to observe three days of mourning after scores killed in high-speed train collision</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98d5c50ce8830f5cf178fee398fe6342f375227e99c78e36de94f67bf739f0fe</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:00:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-two-high-speed-trains-collide-in-southern-spain-rail-operator-says--60afea1444cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-two-high-speed-trains-collide-in-southern-spain-rail-operator-says" /><summary type="html">At least 68 people were killed Wednesday after two high-speed trains collided in Spain's central Toledo province, regional authorities confirmed, with high-speed rail services between Madrid and Andalusia suspended. It is Spain's second deadly train crash in less than a year. Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said the country would observe three days of mourning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>How student assemblies brought down the Serbian government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d269d85ef63bd859516867f0b039fec62bd57e0ffbabe3dea2ae9ea3f9f9071</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:58:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government--6491312ad54a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government" /><summary type="html">A list of academics, engineers, artists and activists chosen by Serbia’s student assemblies defeated long-ruling president Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing Serbian Progressive Party Sunday. The shock victory comes after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests – and may serve as a model for other movements hoping to turn street demonstrations into concrete political change.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France: Lawmakers hold a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi, victim of racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b8b323d5e33083475aeffaf25be86bad4d32c59f68b287bac83ab00d21b17b3</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T17:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1--d1f12ab1013c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1" /><summary type="html">French lawmakers held a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi. The victim of a racist attack died in a shooting last week, while at least five other people were wounded, including a 12-years-old girl. FRANCE 24’s Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Senate takes on the 'rioters pay' bill after protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f2e960573d96eebfcb80207d581272a3a7d3fa41a8910f3f05e1f84cde33362</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:13:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests--b3c03807dca7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests" /><summary type="html">If the French Senate passes this bill, rioters will have to pay for the damage caused during the recent unrest across the country. This "casseurs-payeurs" bill comes in the wake of nationwide violence. This draft law now has an explosive add-on aimed at social media. Senators will vote on whether the government can block platforms that are too slow to act on authorities' reports of dangerous content.</summary></entry><entry><title>Localised Russia-Ukraine ceasefire starts in Ukrainian town facing starvation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64773c18c1a021b9d5e869185d927d8888bbc27eceea26ff2a85407357ad0329</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:34:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation--26b8d037fc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation" /><summary type="html">A localised ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia took effect early Tuesday (October 27) ahead of a humanitarian mission led by US first lady Melania Trump, as missile attacks resumed in Kyiv. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Emmanuelle Chaze, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane delivers emotional acceptance speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3988525fd9f978e8cd5bd8c6f919004ffbe1fa88e0c5f2af8307e07844b1fc4c</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:20:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech--113fa0f87132.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech" /><summary type="html">Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday. Kane scored 73 goals for club and country last campaign and smashed scoring records at the World Cup, where he captained England to a third-place finish.</summary></entry><entry><title>French protests: Student union leaders vow to keep mobilising</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5dafbc61db877f99a992f47d929f2a40078f205dcce7f7b035061e08a9b14c3</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising--5057a3ae5412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising" /><summary type="html">In France, after weeks of student unrest, the government announced new school measures. Student union leaders said it's a first step but vowed to keep mobilising as they expected further proposals.</summary></entry></feed>
